1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:50,592
There's another reason why
you want Mikoy gone so badly.

2
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:51,551
Like what?

3
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,804
And you think,

4
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:57,682
you can make me do what you want because
I'm under your spell.

5
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:09,319
As far as I know,
she's connected to Chiara Valtrovi.

6
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:14,324
And if her information is correct,
then we can take her down.

7
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:23,958
They want something in return.

8
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:29,547
I'm here to ask for your help.

9
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:33,676
Tell me everything you know!

10
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:37,597
But I can take you
to someone who knows where they are.

11
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,474
- Who?
- Vicky Corales.

12
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:40,642
She's known as,

13
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:41,684
Widow's Maid.

14
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:49,317
The tracker I planted on you,
has been activated, Chiara.

15
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:01,079
<i>Looks like my sweetheart</i>
<i>still hasn't changed.</i>

16
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:05,416
If I didn't know you,
I'd think you're still that waiter…

17
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:37,115
Follow me.

18
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:17,363
Well, I guess,

19
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:18,531
you have changed.

20
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,241
A little.

21
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:25,163
Looks like I'm at a disadvantage
in this fight.

22
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:28,207
Dad Mario would be so proud.

23
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:31,127
How dare you even say his name?

24
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:34,464
We treated you like family.

25
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,133
I loved you,

26
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,136
unconditionally.

27
00:03:43,514 --> 00:03:45,308
And then you killed my father.

28
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:05,828
If only I had known,
and if I could turn back time,

29
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,166
So I'm just supposed to forgive you?

30
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:14,754
Just forget everything?

31
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,131
That wasn't what I meant.

32
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:22,720
I'm not stupid!

33
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:23,763
Okay?

34
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:26,391
Tell me,

35
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:30,103
why I shouldn't blow
your brains out right now.

36
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:36,943
Where are Mikoy and Chiara?

37
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:39,779
Are you going to talk,
or do you want to get hurt?

38
00:04:44,075 --> 00:04:45,743
Let's all calm down.

39
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:48,871
I know you want to find Mikoy and Chiara.

40
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:51,958
But this isn't the way
to extract information from her.

41
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:54,669
But I'm running out of time,

42
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:57,088
I need to extract the information I need.

43
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,634
At this point,

44
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,430
Mom, please.

45
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:08,099
Don't say anything if
you don't have anything good to say.

46
00:05:15,606 --> 00:05:17,608
I already spoke with Agent Dara.

47
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:30,580
This isn't just about Dad Mario.

48
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:35,084
You're angry

49
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:37,754
because you think I abandoned you.

50
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:47,263
Why? Isn't it true?

51
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:52,018
You only used me for your ambition.

52
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,312
You manipulated me.

53
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:57,482
You don't love me.

54
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:02,612
for what you really wanted,

55
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,656
to rule over criminals!

56
00:06:09,285 --> 00:06:11,329
You think so little of me, sweetheart.

57
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:18,961
I'm done with all your games.

58
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:23,716
I'm done with you making a fool of me.

59
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,687
I did that

60
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:39,857
so you wouldn't get dragged
into my messed-up life!

61
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:42,944
Because if I kept fighting for our love,

62
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:45,404
you'd only get hurt even more!

63
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:47,573
And I'd never forgive myself

64
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,367
if anything happened to you!

65
00:06:56,874 --> 00:06:58,000
Enough, Chiara.

66
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:01,003
I'm tired of all your lies.

67
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:03,714
Now,

68
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:07,385
you'll pay for everything you've done.

69
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:20,440
Looks like nothing can change
your mind, sweetheart.

70
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:57,894
I'll use this

71
00:07:57,977 --> 00:07:59,645
to make you feel

72
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:02,023
what you did to my father.

73
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,549
That's why I targeted it.

74
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:30,968
Now you'll have a hard time moving,

75
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:32,637
and the advantage is mine.

76
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,775
Looks like we're evenly matched now.

77
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:04,627
Why?

78
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:11,008
Why did you turn your back on me?

79
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,490
But I only ended up hurting you more.

80
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,888
I never should've met you.

81
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:00,349
I never should've

82
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:03,227
dragged you into my world.

83
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:15,072
I promise,

84
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:17,908
I will never stop

85
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:20,328
loving you.

86
00:11:27,603 --> 00:11:28,646
Chiara!

87
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,360
Chiara, are you okay?

88
00:11:40,991 --> 00:11:42,701
Leave me here as a decoy!

89
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,245
After everything you've done?

90
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:45,579
Now you want to play the hero?

91
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:54,004
We have to fight.

92
00:11:58,008 --> 00:11:59,552
We don't have a choice

93
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:00,678
because I'm not leaving you.

94
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:02,346
We'll both end up dead!

95
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:07,518
But we still have a chance.

96
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:10,688
After all,
La Fornarina is on my side again.

97
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:14,859
Okay. Well, that makes me feel confident.

98
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:16,610
Because apparently,

99
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:18,612
I'm backed by the
Philippines' national drunkard.

100
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:45,681
You idiot, Mikoy.

101
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:47,850
Don't you dare die.

102
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:49,977
Wait for me.

103
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:06,243
Looks like we screwed up, my love.

104
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:24,220
We wasted so much time.

105
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:31,101
Because even if it wasn't forever…

106
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:42,947
Find me.

107
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:57,182
Senator Quintin.

108
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:02,479
I'm sorry,
but there's a warrant for your arrest.

109
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,318
Is this a joke?

110
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:12,072
Wait, wait, wait!

111
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:13,741
What is this? This isn't real!

112
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:15,242
I'm innocent!

113
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:17,327
I'm not a member of any syndicate!

114
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:18,245
This is bullshit!

115
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:20,539
Give me that.

116
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:22,249
Put the handcuffs on him.

117
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:23,667
Handcuffs? Is this a prank?

118
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:31,050
<i>Agent Djanggo.</i>

119
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:41,018
<i>You have the right to remain silent.</i>

120
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:45,105
<i>Anything you say may be used against you.</i>

121
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:47,107
With the death of Chiara Valtrovi,

122
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:49,693
we thought it was a dead
end for the agency.

123
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,279
Well, apparently,

124
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:54,948
she had set up

125
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:58,035
what we call in law enforcement

126
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:00,662
a dead man's switch.

127
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:05,918
In the event of her death…

128
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:22,726
<i>…that conducted the pursuit and arrest</i>

129
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:25,646
<i>of Concordat officials and leaders.</i>

130
00:18:25,729 --> 00:18:29,108
<i>We have arrested hundreds</i>
<i>of significant figures</i>

131
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:31,151
<i>from various syndicates.</i>

132
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:32,861
<i>Not only in Europe,</i>

133
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:35,572
<i>but also in Asia and the Middle East.</i>

134
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:49,336
And Chiara didn't just provide information
about the key figures.

135
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,281
Good for you. And…

136
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:23,287
You're free.

137
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,080
Mom, please.

138
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:28,375
I just wanted to know if you were okay.

139
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:31,753
I would've been better
if my own daughter hadn't screwed me over.

140
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:34,339
Mom, what's done is done.

141
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:36,758
Be angry if you want.

142
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:40,220
But as for me,

143
00:19:40,804 --> 00:19:41,889
I'll always be here,

144
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:45,893
and I'll always be your son.

145
00:19:52,357 --> 00:19:53,400
You better.

146
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,695
You're the one who put me here.

147
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:00,908
So make sure

148
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:04,244
you visit me every day.

149
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:10,542
I'll never leave you, Mom.

150
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:16,548
By the way, what happened
to Chiara and Mikoy?

151
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:21,261
Mikoy and Chiara are dead!

152
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:23,889
Because of your illegal operations!

153
00:20:23,972 --> 00:20:26,391
And your deal with Vickey Corales.

154
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:27,851
That's not true!

155
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:29,895
I know you know

156
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:31,688
that Mikoy and Chiara are still alive.

157
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:46,620
Chiara! Mikoy!

158
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:52,251
Medic! Call a medic! Hurry!

159
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:54,711
<i>I know Mikoy and Chiara are still alive!</i>

160
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:57,005
Whether Mikoy and Chiara are
dead or alive…

161
00:20:59,591 --> 00:21:03,220
Because I'll make sure you rot in prison!

162
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:07,432
Mikoy and Chiara are still alive!

163
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:15,691
They're still alive!

164
00:21:18,235 --> 00:21:19,194
Carlota!

165
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:23,156
So, General, what you're trying to tell me

166
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:25,951
is that Chiara went back to the Concordat,

167
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:29,121
not to betray us or Mikoy, but

168
00:21:29,913 --> 00:21:33,292
to discover the ins and
outs of their operation?

169
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:35,961
Maybe so she could take them down too?
Right?

170
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:45,053
Cliche as it may seem,

171
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:47,097
she was able to bring down

172
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:50,058
some of the biggest syndicates…

173
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:04,323
Are Chiara and Mikoy truly dead?

174
00:22:21,256 --> 00:22:22,966
I hope wherever you are, Dad,

175
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:25,719
you are proud of me.

176
00:22:33,643 --> 00:22:36,605
Because my mission is to continue yours.

177
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:41,068
Thank you, Dad.

178
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,404
Thank you for always watching over me.

179
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:48,158
Give Mom a kiss for me.

180
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:12,516
I'm sure she'll be pissed.

181
00:23:32,285 --> 00:23:36,623
We should demand
to repatriate Chiara’s body.

182
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:39,000
You might be forgetting…

183
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:52,764
What?

184
00:23:59,020 --> 00:23:59,980
Maybe,

185
00:24:00,063 --> 00:24:02,482
Chiara and Mikoy are still alive.

186
00:24:03,942 --> 00:24:05,861
What are you talking about?
You know you're just hungry.

187
00:24:05,944 --> 00:24:07,737
Where's our order? Hold on.

188
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:08,905
Waiter.

189
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:36,224
Why?

190
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:37,893
Why did you suddenly space out?
What happened?

191
00:25:15,847 --> 00:25:17,515
Let's go!

192
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:21,269
- Let's go in here. Here.
- Hey, wait!

193
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:22,979
Let me play too, Chiara!

194
00:25:23,688 --> 00:25:25,106
What are you talking about?

195
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:27,108
Someone might hear you!

196
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,318
Pepito, come on!

197
00:25:28,401 --> 00:25:29,611
Oh, right!

198
00:25:30,195 --> 00:25:31,196
Clara!

199
00:25:31,279 --> 00:25:33,240
See what you did?

200
00:25:42,332 --> 00:25:43,291
Only this small?

201
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:47,295
Grandma's here!

202
00:25:47,379 --> 00:25:48,588
Grandma's here!

203
00:25:48,672 --> 00:25:49,631
Let's go!

204
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:52,968
- Let's eat. Come on.
- Thanks, Mom.

205
00:25:53,051 --> 00:25:55,011
- Let's eat.
- It's time to eat. Let's go.

206
00:25:55,929 --> 00:25:57,138
Rice cakes!

207
00:25:57,222 --> 00:25:58,223
Is that good?

208
00:25:58,306 --> 00:25:59,182
Yes, it's delicious!

209
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:00,767
You'll forget your own name!

210
00:26:00,850 --> 00:26:02,185
Then let's buy some!

211
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:04,229
- What's that?
- I'll take one!

212
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:05,981
Will you two stop it?

213
00:26:06,064 --> 00:26:07,857
Later. That's for dessert.

214
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:09,359
Just one.

215
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:12,320
Fine, we'll buy them all.

216
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:14,197
Mikoy, the food's ready.

217
00:26:14,823 --> 00:26:16,408
I told you not to say that!

218
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,411
Oh, right. You're not Mikoy anymore.

219
00:26:19,494 --> 00:26:20,537
You said it again!

220
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:21,997
You're Pepito now!

221
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:24,958
Didn't I tell you not to
use Mikoy anymore, Bro?

222
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:26,626
You said it too!

223
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:29,713
Hey, enough with the neck slaps!

224
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,340
Come on, let's eat! Let's go!

225
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:33,675
- Okay, Mom.
- Yes, Tess!

226
00:26:33,758 --> 00:26:35,218
- I'll just pay for this.
- There!

227
00:26:36,970 --> 00:26:38,805
- Thanks, Bro!
- Thank you, thank you po.

228
00:26:38,888 --> 00:26:40,098
This is really good, huh?

229
00:26:41,725 --> 00:26:43,601
- Let's eat!
- There we go, come on!

230
00:26:43,685 --> 00:26:44,728
Time to eat!

231
00:26:44,811 --> 00:26:46,688
Mikoy, Chiara, come on!

232
00:26:46,771 --> 00:26:48,398
Sofie!

233
00:26:48,481 --> 00:26:52,068
I told you never to say that!

234
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:54,029
Come on, Ka Pepe!

235
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:55,822
Enough with all the head-slapping!

236
00:26:55,905 --> 00:26:57,365
With all the knocking on your heads,

237
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:59,534
you might all turn into dummies!

238
00:26:59,617 --> 00:27:01,161
That would be great, Mom!

239
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:03,079
So they won't forget

240
00:27:03,163 --> 00:27:04,998
that they can't call Sis and Bro

241
00:27:05,081 --> 00:27:06,458
by their old names anymore.

242
00:27:07,334 --> 00:27:08,585
It's the secret

243
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:11,087
of the Pinagpalas.

244
00:27:12,464 --> 00:27:13,965
Oh, come on!

245
00:27:14,049 --> 00:27:16,426
You're the only Pinagpala here, Angelito!

246
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:18,636
- Tess!
- You’re too flirty!

247
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:19,804
Tess!

248
00:27:20,513 --> 00:27:22,265
- Dekyo!
- We have a visitor!

249
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:24,476
- Who?
- Who is it?

250
00:27:25,393 --> 00:27:26,686
- Wow!
- Wow!

251
00:27:27,562 --> 00:27:28,688
Mario.

252
00:27:28,772 --> 00:27:31,191
You know, you're really sweet, Dekyo.

253
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:32,609
A little weird, but sweet.

254
00:27:33,318 --> 00:27:34,361
Thank you, Tess.

255
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:35,528
Come on, let's eat,

256
00:27:35,612 --> 00:27:36,780
before the flies get to it!

257
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:39,574
- Mario, they said to eat!
- Yes. Let's eat.

258
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:41,618
Oops, before we eat,

259
00:27:41,701 --> 00:27:43,745
I just want to get everyone's attention.

260
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:47,040
I just want to say

261
00:27:48,166 --> 00:27:50,627
I'm happy I became part of this family.

262
00:27:51,795 --> 00:27:54,756
That, this is the family
I've always dreamed of.

263
00:27:55,632 --> 00:27:57,509
Oh, come on!

264
00:27:57,592 --> 00:27:59,636
Our Rahmboy really is something, huh?

265
00:27:59,719 --> 00:28:01,930
He even has a dramatic speech!

266
00:28:02,013 --> 00:28:03,139
You know,

267
00:28:03,223 --> 00:28:05,558
no crying at the dinner table!

268
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:08,186
- Come here, baby boy! You need a hug.
- Come here!

269
00:28:08,269 --> 00:28:09,854
You need a hug from mommy!

270
00:28:09,938 --> 00:28:12,107
Come on. Join us.

271
00:28:12,190 --> 00:28:13,775
Perfect, the food is ready.

272
00:28:13,858 --> 00:28:15,318
- Hey! That's… The agents!
- Hello!

273
00:28:15,402 --> 00:28:16,611
Agent Alex!

274
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:20,156
‪-Hey!
‪-Hi!

275
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:23,451
Sorry to interrupt, but

276
00:28:27,956 --> 00:28:29,416
These are your credentials.

277
00:28:29,499 --> 00:28:31,042
Your new identities.

278
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:32,669
Your identities are different,

279
00:28:32,752 --> 00:28:35,422
but at least you can live
normal lives now.

280
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:38,299
The agency also wants to thank you.

281
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:44,764
‪-Take that!
‪-Shut it.

282
00:28:46,057 --> 00:28:48,101
Sorry about that.

283
00:28:48,184 --> 00:28:51,187
It's just a reminder that from now on,

284
00:28:51,271 --> 00:28:55,525
we should be called
Mr. Pepito and Mrs. Lara

285
00:28:55,608 --> 00:28:56,526
Pinaglaban!

286
00:28:57,652 --> 00:28:58,570
Wow!

287
00:28:58,653 --> 00:29:00,113
Pinaglaban.

288
00:29:00,697 --> 00:29:02,907
That's right. From now on,

289
00:29:03,658 --> 00:29:07,078
the names Mikoy and Chiara are forbidden!

290
00:29:07,620 --> 00:29:08,580
‪Take that too!

291
00:29:09,581 --> 00:29:11,040
- Why?
- That's two names!

292
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:12,250
Enough with the head-slapping.

293
00:29:12,333 --> 00:29:14,002
Come on, let's eat!

294
00:29:14,085 --> 00:29:15,879
- Yes, let's go!
- Oh, don't mind us.

295
00:29:15,962 --> 00:29:17,505
We won't stay long,

296
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:18,548
we just stopped by.

297
00:29:18,631 --> 00:29:20,175
Besides, we're not ready for the beach.

298
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:21,718
- What?
- You're not going to swim?

299
00:29:21,801 --> 00:29:23,178
We're leaving already?

300
00:29:23,261 --> 00:29:24,304
Why?

301
00:29:24,387 --> 00:29:27,056
Can't we go swimming
for a little while first?

302
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:29,267
Oh, no! We can't let this day end

303
00:29:29,350 --> 00:29:30,351
without swimming, okay?

304
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:32,020
You two are going swimming!

305
00:29:32,103 --> 00:29:33,438
Let's go swimming!

306
00:29:33,521 --> 00:29:34,939
- Let's go!
- Wow!

307
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:38,067
- I thought you weren't ready?
- Not ready, huh?

308
00:29:41,488 --> 00:29:42,655
Tess.

309
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:43,823
Actually, I'm still full!

310
00:29:43,907 --> 00:29:45,742
- We're not hungry!
- We'll go swimming first!

311
00:29:45,825 --> 00:29:47,076
That floatie's huge!

312
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,536
All of these are ours now, Tess.

313
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:49,829
Okay!

314
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:51,915
- Hey, I'm coming too!
- Here.

315
00:29:52,916 --> 00:29:54,292
- Come on, let's eat.
- Come on, eat up.

316
00:29:54,375 --> 00:29:56,711
- Agent Alex.
- Agent Alex, come here!

317
00:29:57,462 --> 00:29:58,588
Join us, Alex.

318
00:29:58,671 --> 00:30:00,006
Come eat with us!

319
00:30:00,089 --> 00:30:01,591
There's so much food!

320
00:30:07,931 --> 00:30:09,974
Where's my thing, anyone?

321
00:30:10,058 --> 00:30:11,810
You know what would make it even better?

322
00:30:13,436 --> 00:30:14,270
What?

323
00:30:16,189 --> 00:30:17,357
No!

324
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:20,652
I'm watching a classic
Filipino film rerun now…
